KZ2 patch 6087: the frame thread sleeps on POSIX hosts.

Written for the Pyrrhus native Mac bring-up; no game code or RPCS3 code used.
Licence: MIT (project LICENSE).

cellGcm_walker_wait was a no-op everywhere but Windows -- (void)ms; return 0; -- so
on the Mac route the frame thread spun at the outer loop's full rate: ~8 kHz drain
passes, ~35k message pumps a second (each a dispatch_sync to the main queue; that
was the dominant stack of every walker sample), a busy core and main-queue
contention, all for a loop whose design cadence is one pass per 4 ms. Sleep like
the Windows build does. The acquire fast path (patch 6082's label re-check) needs
no event; a park ends within the sleep exactly as the Windows build's did before
patch 6038 gave it one.

diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
index 2eba5a7..65b1810 100644
